{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO REVIEWS - DATA SOURCE SWITCH
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*** THIS FILE HOLDS THE ONE SWITCH THAT DECIDES WHERE REVIEWS COME FROM. ***

  false -> the baked JSON theme assets + assets/aao-reviews.js  (the original system, still live)
  true  -> Shopify metaobjects, server-rendered by Liquid       (the new system)

Flip `use_metaobjects` to true ONCE the metaobject definitions and entries exist and the product
metafields are populated. See docs/reviews/README.md and the migration spec.

Why a snippet and not an `assign` in aao-reviews-boot.liquid: `{% render %}` gives a snippet an
isolated scope, so a variable set in the boot snippet is invisible to the widget and the badge.
A snippet's OUTPUT, however, can be captured by any caller:

    {%- capture aao_mode -%}{%- render 'aao-reviews-flags' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if aao_mode contains 'metaobjects' -%} ... {%- endif -%}

so this file stays the single source of truth for all three snippets.

Emits exactly one word and nothing else. Do not add markup here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign use_metaobjects = true

  if use_metaobjects
    echo 'metaobjects'
  else
    echo 'json'
  endif
-%}
